{"entryId":"3417","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3417:1","sourceSha256":"94f5cd3a762f58906ab66095c0bfb8143669de7c2e9ad696e3a5197a4ff18917","englishSha256":"496f3d6b70e4de98fddfbcc9131e7a95bd640cd6f970bcb30f266c9fec1ab9dc","citations":[{"id":"3417:1:link-005","he":[81,96],"en":[159,169],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_8.1"},"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 8:1","assessment":"The Mishnah names Shimon’s testimony and Akiva’s addition. Yehoshua is named in 8:1, while Yehudah is named separately with Yehoshua at 8:3.","evidence":[{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 8:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_8.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"},{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 8:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_8.3"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]},{"id":"3417:1:link-006","he":[97,112],"en":[170,199],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_23b.8"},"reference":"Chagigah 23b:8","assessment":"The checked folio takes up Akiva’s addition in the discussion of contamination, citing the same Mishnah.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chagigah 23b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_23b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chagigah 23b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chagigah_23b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3417:1:link-007","he":[177,193],"en":[303,332],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_3a.11.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 3a:11:1","assessment":"Rashi discusses the form Ben Beteira as Yehoshua’s patronymic. The quoted gloss does not name Shimon or directly assign the group that installed Hillel.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 3a:11:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_3a.11.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 3a:12:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_3a.12.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Rashi on Taanit 3a:12:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Taanit_3a.12.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3417:1:link-008","he":[233,260],"en":[406,457],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_66a.3"},"reference":"Pesachim 66a:3","assessment":"Pesachim directly says the Benei Beteira appointed Hillel. It gives no personal names in that narrative.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 66a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_66a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 66a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_66a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3417:1:link-009","he":[281,311],"en":[485,531],"target":{"entry":1619,"paragraph":3},"reference":"Seder HaDorot, Tanaim and Amoraim 1619:3","assessment":"The earlier entry reports the Rashi attribution and explicitly challenges the chronology by comparing other witnesses.","evidence":[{"reference":"Seder HaDorot 1619:3","target":{"entry":1619,"paragraph":3},"witness":"Pinned Warsaw digital witness"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4],"holds":[{"raw":"ושכח לר' שמעון זה","reason":"The narrator’s complaint assumes these notices concern one generation. The checked appointment story is collective, and the named Mishnah testimonies cannot settle that chronology.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 66a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_66a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Mishnah Eduyot 8:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Mishnah_Eduyot_8.1"},"witness":"Torat Emet 357"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"Eduyot 8:1 names Yehoshua and Shimon. Yehudah is named with Yehoshua later, in 8:3.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
